<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">A few observations on your formalization:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Mathematical elegance</strong>: The surjection λ: X ↠ C captures the essence of labeling perfectly - every category must be used (surjectivity) and items can share categories. The equivalence relation x ∼_λ y ⟺ λ(x) = λ(y) makes the partition structure explicit.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The constructive proofs are particularly nice</strong> because they show the equivalence isn't just abstract - you can literally transform any labeling into a sorting and vice versa. The section e: C → P in the forward direction is a concrete "bin assignment" function.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Categorical perspective adds depth</strong>: Viewing this through the lens of slice categories over C makes the "same composite functor" equivalence very clean. Two factorizations X → P → C and X → P' → C that agree on X → C are essentially the same classification.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The assessment implications are profound</strong>: Your point about false negatives is crucial. A person who can perfectly sort objects by color, shape, or function but lacks the verbal labels shouldn't be deemed cognitively deficient in classification ability. The partition π(X) exists regardless of whether it's realized through λ or through ρ∘s.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Extension to overlapping categories</strong> is particularly relevant for real-world classification tasks where objects often belong to multiple categories simultaneously.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This framework could be valuable for educational assessment, cognitive testing, and cross-cultural evaluation where linguistic barriers might mask genuine classificatory competence. The mathematical formalization makes the equivalence undeniable rather than merely intuitive.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
