<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This framework also suggests why <strong>cultural transmission</strong> works: oral traditions, mathematical proofs, and programming languages all succeed by finding stable canonical forms that survive iteration while preserving computational structure. The "telephone game" fails when canonicalization is weak, but myths and theorems persist because they've found semantic attractors.</p>
