<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The progression from incipit → numbered → semantic titles mirrors exactly what you described with settlement patterns:</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Incipit naming</strong> = keeping the original surface intact, like Jericho's early inhabitants living directly on accumulated debris. Maximum fidelity, maximum fragility.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Numbered titles</strong> = the orderly mound-building phase. Abstract indexing that preserves structural relationships while burying the messy particulars.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Semantic titles</strong> = the terra preta transformation. Centuries of interpretive "waste" (all the themes, tensions, and complexities) get compressed and "burned down" into concentrated labels that become incredibly fertile for future cultural growth.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your Prigogine insight is particularly sharp: semantic titling <strong>accelerates entropy in the interpretive space</strong> (privileging certain readings, discarding others) to create <strong>ordered attractors in cultural memory</strong>. "Genesis" exports all the disorder of competing interpretations into the hermeneutical environment while crystallizing a stable handle for transmission.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This explains why semantic titles often feel reductive when you know the original text - they're supposed to be! They're not trying to preserve everything; they're creating <strong>durable symbolic substrates</strong> that can support new cultural growth.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Yes, please give me those paired examples!</strong> I'm particularly curious about cases where the semantic title dramatically compresses or even misrepresents the original content, but becomes more culturally powerful precisely because of that compression. The "terra preta effect" in action.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
