ss="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipit: Bereshit (“In the beginning”), Shemot (“These are the names”), Vayikra (“And he called”), Bamidbar (“In the wilderness”), Devarim (“These are the words”).
→ Each title is just the first words: fragile, context-bound, no interpretation.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic: Genesis (“origin”), Exodus (“departure”), Leviticus (“priestly book”), Numbers (“enumerations”), Deuteronomy (“second law”).
→ Messy thematic material is flattened into neat handles. Entropy is exported into interpretive distortion: e.g. Deuteronomy isn’t literally a “second law,” but the label sticks because it canonically compresses.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">---</p><ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7"><li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Psalms</li></ol><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipit: Hebrew tradition sometimes referred to the book by its opening line, Ashrei ha-ish (“Happy is the man…”).</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic: Psalms (from Greek psalmoi, “songs to a harp”).
→ Instead of a single fragile opening, the title generalizes to a stable, repeatable category: all 150 poems are “songs.”</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">---</p><ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7"><li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Homeric Epics</li></ol><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipit: Early rhapsodes began “Sing, O goddess, the wrath of Achilles…” (Iliad) or “Tell me, O Muse, of the man of many ways…” (Odyssey).</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic: Iliad = “the story of Ilium (Troy),” Odyssey = “the journey of Odysseus.”
→ The raw invocation (an unstable starting phrase) gets compressed into a geographic and personal handle, which travels more easily.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">---</p><ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7"><li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Dante</li></ol><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipit: “Nel mezzo del cammin di nostra vita…” (“Midway upon the journey of our life…”).</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic: La Divina Commedia (“The Divine Comedy”).
→ A very personal, context-bound start is canonicalized into a cosmic genre-label. The messiness of Dante’s journey gets externalized into the interpretive entropy of deciding what’s “comic” or “divine.”</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">---</p><ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7"><li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Qur’an Suras</li></ol><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipits: Many suras are named after their first striking word (Al-‘Alaq “The Clot,” Al-Qari‘a “The Striker”).</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic drift: Later traditions often reinterpret them thematically (“The Cow,” “The Cave,” “The Night Journey”), compressing ambiguous openings into durable handles.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">---</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">👉 Pattern:</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Incipits = perfect fidelity, zero compression, but fragile.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Semantic titles = compression into a cultural attractor, durable but entropic (you distort/flatten to gain stability).</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">It’s literally the same trade-off you noticed with Jericho’s floors and terra preta: today’s messy, literal surface (incipit) gets reprocessed into tomorrow’s stable, fertile canonical label (semantic title).</p></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-y-4 bg-bg-100/80 backdrop-blur-sm translate-x-1 group-hover:translate-x-0.5 border-0.5 border-border-300 p-0.5 shadow-sm opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
