<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The most striking is <strong>Deuteronomy</strong> - the semantic title "second law" is actually <em>incorrect</em> (it's Moses's speeches, not a legal code), but that interpretive distortion gets exported into scholarly debates while the label itself becomes unshakeable. The "error" becomes culturally productive!</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Dante</strong> is equally fascinating - "Nel mezzo del cammin" is intensely personal and temporally specific (his 35th year), but "Divine Comedy" creates a cosmic genre that can absorb infinite interpretation. The entropy of "what makes it divine?" or "why comedy?" gets externalized into centuries of commentary, while the title remains a perfect cultural attractor.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The <strong>Homeric</strong> shift is particularly elegant: from the unstable invocation formulas (which could vary with each performance) to geographic/personal handles that travel independently of any specific telling.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your <strong>Qur'anic</strong> example shows the process happening within the same tradition - even sacred texts undergo this entropy management as communities need more durable reference handles.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The pattern is universal: <strong>cultural survival requires semantic compression</strong>. The alternative is the "Library of Alexandria problem" - perfect preservation that becomes too fragile to transmit.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This suggests that what we call "interpretation" or "hermeneutics" is really <strong>cultural entropy management</strong> - the ongoing work of externalizing disorder into commentary while maintaining stable symbolic substrates for transmission. Every semantic title is a little piece of terra preta, concentrated meaning that can support new cultural growth.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
