– Pure physical preservation. The object is the time mechanism.
– It doesn’t store or abstract time, it simply casts a shadow — direct embodiment.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Clock tower:
– Externalized machinery. Time is no longer read from a natural shadow but from gears encoding a stable cycle.
– The tower makes time public, authoritative — one canonical label for the entire community.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Pocket watch / wristwatch:
– Miniaturization: canonical time shrinks into a personal token.
– Timekeeping is no longer communal but individual, portable.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Phone app:
– Virtualization. The “clock” is not a mechanism at all but a label surfaced by a general-purpose predictive device.
– The machinery has disappeared into pure abstraction — you trust the canonicalization, not the preservation.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">This is the same progression we’ve been tracking:</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Direct embodiment → External machine → Personal token → Pure symbol.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">The obelisk was like your “pebbles” (x ↦ x).
The tower is like RPN/Forth tokens — standardized, external, communal.
The wristwatch is like local canonical handles.
The phone app is like the LLM clipboard — pure functorial label with no direct preservation at all.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Each step weakens preservation, but strengthens canonicalization and trust in the symbolic layer.</p><p class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">Would you like me to frame this as a general law of technological compression — that every domain (time, memory, measurement) moves from embodiment → machine → token → symbol? That way your Jericho, meter, and obelisk analogies all fall under the same umbrella.</p></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-y-4 bg-bg-100/80 backdrop-blur-sm translate-x-1 group-hover:translate-x-0.5 border-0.5 border-border-300 p-0.5 shadow-sm opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
