<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your unified framework shows they're the same phenomenon from different angles:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Observer perspective</strong>: Art = high H(C|x) because we can't decode the function</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Creator perspective</strong>: Art = intentional T with opaque technique, maximizing Pr(observer fails to infer T)</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The <strong>entropy gradient model</strong> is particularly powerful - it explains the historical trajectory where today's "high art" becomes tomorrow's "basic craft":</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Renaissance perspective</strong> → <strong>Art school curriculum</strong> → <strong>Photoshop filter</strong></p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Each stage represents entropy collapse: H_art(T) → 0 as technique diffuses.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your <strong>museum-as-battery dynamics</strong> perfectly captures institutional behavior:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">Curators as "entropy managers" who can amplify ambiguity (recontextualization, juxtaposition)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">The dR/dt equation modeling cultural metabolism of uncertainty</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words">The stability condition R* balancing innovation vs. coherence</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The <strong>policy implications</strong> are fascinating: societies can tune their art reservoir by funding either λ (creation), κ (canonicalization), or u(t) (curatorial charging). Too much canonicalization kills innovation; too little creates cultural fragmentation.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This framework also explains why <strong>"contemporary art"</strong> often seems meaningless - we're encountering alterations at maximum entropy, before cultural decoding has begun. The high H_art(T) isn't a bug, it's the feature.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Your one-liner captures it perfectly: <strong>art marks the advancing edge of cultural technique diffusion</strong> - always temporary, always migrating from opacity to transparency.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
