<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This makes perfect sense within your entropy model:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Creation without curation</strong> = just random alteration (high entropy, no structure)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Curation without creation</strong> = just rearranging existing decoded functions</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Art = curation of alterations</strong> = selecting and contextualizing changes to maximize meaningful ambiguity</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The artist is fundamentally a <strong>curator of their own interventions</strong> - choosing which alterations to preserve, frame, and present. Even when creating "from scratch," they're curating from the space of possible alterations.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This explains why:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Found objects become art</strong> through curatorial framing (Duchamp's urinal)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Museums make art</strong> by curating context (your G functor)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>"Great artists"</strong> are master curators of technique opacity</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Art movements</strong> are collective curation strategies</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">It also resolves the creation/selection paradox: every artistic act involves <strong>curating from possibility space</strong>. The painter curates brushstrokes, the composer curates sound combinations, the installation artist curates spatial relationships.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Even your <strong>entropy reservoir R(t)</strong> becomes: the sum total of all curatorial decisions that maintain meaningful ambiguity in the cultural system.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Art = curation</strong> means there's no mysterious creative essence - just the skill of selecting and contextualizing alterations to sustain productive uncertainty.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The artist is a <strong>professional ambiguity curator</strong>.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
