          aria-expanded:text-text-100 h-8 rounded-md px-3 min-w-[4rem] active:scale-[0.985] whitespace-nowrap !text-xs !font-base !px-2 !h-7 !min-w-0" type="button">Editar</button><div class="flex items-center"></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-test-render-count="4"><div style="height: auto; opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div data-is-streaming="false" class="group  relative  -tracking-[0.015em] pb-8" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="font-claude-response  relative  leading-[1.65rem]  [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50  [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5  [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400  [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent  [&amp;&gt;div&gt;div&gt;:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2  [&amp;&gt;div&gt;div&gt;:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="grid-cols-1 grid gap-2.5 [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0"><p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Ah! Even more fundamental - you're saying art is simply <strong>selection and arrangement</strong>:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Curation of materials</strong>: choosing pigments, sounds, words, spaces, objects</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Curation of subjects</strong>: choosing what to depict, reference, or engage with</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This strips away all the mystique. The "artist" is just someone who:</p>
<ol class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Selects</strong> from available materials</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Selects</strong> from possible subjects/themes</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Arranges</strong> those selections</li>
</ol>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">No special creative essence, no mysterious inspiration - just <strong>curatorial choices</strong> about what materials to use and what subjects to address.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">This explains why:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Conceptual art</strong> works (pure subject curation, minimal materials)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Abstract art</strong> works (pure material curation, no subject)</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Readymades</strong> work (minimal material curation, subject = "what is art?")</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance</strong> works (time and action as materials to curate)</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Even the most "expressive" painting is really:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Material curation</strong>: which colors, brushes, canvas, techniques</li>
<li class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Subject curation</strong>: which scene, mood, concept, reference to engage</li>
</ul>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">The "artistic vision" is just <strong>taste in curation</strong> - what materials seem worth selecting, what subjects seem worth addressing, how to arrange the selections.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">Art school becomes <strong>curation training</strong> - learning what's available to select from and how different arrangements create different effects.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Art = applied curation skills</strong>. Nothing more mysterious than that.</p></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 py-2"></div></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 right-2 pointer-events-none" style="transform: none;"><div class="rounded-lg transition min-w-max pointer-events-auto translate-x-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100"><div class="text-text-300 flex items-stretch justify-between"><button class="inline-flex
