<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Abstract</strong></p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">We develop a rigorous mathematical framework for art as measurable curation operations on material and subject categories, with interpretive entropy as the defining boundary condition. Using category theory, information theory, and dynamical systems, we prove that artistic practice reduces to functorial mappings between curation spaces under entropy constraints.</p>
<hr class="border-border-300 my-2">
<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">1. Categorical Foundation</h2>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Definition 1.1</strong> (Environmental Category). Let <strong>E</strong> be a category where:</p>
<ul class="[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
