<hr class="border-border-300 my-2">
<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">9. Computational Complexity</h2>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Theorem 9.1</strong>. Optimal curation is NP-hard in general, but admits polynomial-time approximation schemes for bounded entropy budgets.</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Corollary 9.1</strong>. Museum curation reduces to MAX-ENTROPY subject to resource constraints.</p>
